body:
Err, yes it looks like 4138d5aa751bf9c31e8aee3307a513c9b0d49d5a or 8fb707e16dab63609bf29b0eac65cf6395af8942 has broken the dropbox backend.

The integration tests are unhappy too: https://pub.rclone.org/integration-tests/current/

@mathieucarbou have you got time to look at this?

@kernalkue: yes, do not use the latest rclone version. Also, I have sent days ago a PR (#2830) to revert the Dropbox upgrade. It is up to @ncw to merge or not.

If you want a working retry after support for now, then you have to build your own rclone version that includes PR #2830 and #2831 which is supporting retry-after header for some Dropbox API calls but not all.

@ncw: after our moving is finished and we are settled, I should have some time to look at this. But this will be mid/end January....

Also, I don't really understand why the code compiles but fail at runtime with this header, which is in the Dropbox API by the way...
